    "controller_support": "full",
    "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Vulcard, the god of the volcano, is angry. As the two strongest warriors, your mission is to ascend the volcano and follow the ancient tradition to bring an offering to the god himself. In this two-player, time-based, roguelike deckbuilder, you have to collaborate to survive! Choose between different characters with distinct starting decks and unique abilities to fight your way up. Build your deck, meet curious characters, face countless enemies, experience intense boss fights and earn epic rewards! Can you return peace to the island?</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Features</strong></h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Four characters to choose from.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >80+ cards to assemble your deck.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >30+ different enemies.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Real time card battling</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>FAQ</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Can I play this game alone?</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Yes. While the game is intended as a two player game, you can control both characters at once on the same keyboard. We often do this ourselves too when we test things and it provides a bit of an extra challenge to more experienced players.\u00a0</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>What sets Vulcard apart from other roguelike deckbuilders?</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Vulcard is to our knowledge the only roguelike deckbuilder that uses time based combat. This means that enemies don't just wait for you to end your turn and instead regularly attack you, forcing you to make quick decisions. This makes Vulcard a fast-paced and action packed card battling game.</p>",
    "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Vulcard, the god of the volcano, is angry. As the two strongest warriors, your mission is to ascend the volcano and follow the ancient tradition to bring an offering to the god himself. In this two-player, time-based, roguelike deckbuilder, you have to collaborate to survive! Choose between different characters with distinct starting decks and unique abilities to fight your way up. Build your deck, meet curious characters, face countless enemies, experience intense boss fights and earn epic rewards! Can you return peace to the island?</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Features</strong></h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Four characters to choose from.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >80+ cards to assemble your deck.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >30+ different enemies.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Real time card battling</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>FAQ</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Can I play this game alone?</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Yes. While the game is intended as a two player game, you can control both characters at once on the same keyboard. We often do this ourselves too when we test things and it provides a bit of an extra challenge to more experienced players.\u00a0</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>What sets Vulcard apart from other roguelike deckbuilders?</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Vulcard is to our knowledge the only roguelike deckbuilder that uses time based combat. This means that enemies don't just wait for you to end your turn and instead regularly attack you, forcing you to make quick decisions. This makes Vulcard a fast-paced and action packed card battling game.</p>",
    "short_description": "In this two-player, time-based, roguelike deckbuilder, you have to collaborate to survive! Communication is key, but you need to be fast because enemies don't wait for you to end your turn. Devise unique strategies, meet curious creatures and battle your way to the top of the volcano.",
